**What to draw:** a large rectangular block showing the layers from the surface downwards, with ruled label lines and a title: *Diagram of a transverse (vertical) section of the human skin*.

**Parts to draw and label:**

* **Epidermis** (top layer) with the **dead surface layer (stratum corneum)**, the **Malpighian (germinative) layer** below it, and **pigment (melanin) cells**;
* **Hair** (shaft above the surface) and **hair follicle** with the **hair bulb (papilla)**;
* **Erector (arrector pili) muscle** attached to the hair follicle;
* **Sebaceous gland** opening into the follicle;
* **Sweat gland** (coiled tube) and **sweat duct** ending in a **sweat pore** at the surface;
* **Dermis** (middle layer) with **blood capillaries**, an **arteriole and venule**, **sensory nerve endings (receptors for touch, pressure, pain, heat and cold)** and a **sensory nerve fibre**;
* **Subcutaneous fat (adipose tissue)** in the lowest layer, with a blood vessel.
